      "problem": "Solve for $a$ where $c=3a+7b.$",
      "worked_solution": "We need to isolate $a,$ so we will treat the other variables $b$ and $c$ constants. We can use the addition and multiplication principles to solve for $a.$\n\nFirst, we subtract $7b$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =3a+7b \\\\ c-7b & =3a+7b-7b \\\\ c-7b & =3a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides by $3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a & =c-7b \\\\ \\frac{3a}{3} & =\\frac{c-7b}{3} \\\\ a & =\\frac{c-7b}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
